# Stock Research Skill Definition

## Metadata
- **Name:** Stock Research Analysis
- **Version:** 1.0
- **Category:** Finance & Investment
- **Difficulty:** Intermediate
- **Time to Learn:** 5 minutes
- **Time to Use:** 2-3 minutes per analysis

## Description
A comprehensive stock analysis skill that leverages Claude AI to provide 
structured research on any publicly-traded company.

## Inputs
```json
{
  "stock_symbol": "string (e.g., AAPL)",
  "analysis_depth": "string (Quick|Standard|Deep)",
  "optional_context": "string (sector focus, market conditions, etc.)"
}
```

## Outputs
```json
{
  "company_overview": "string",
  "financial_metrics": {
    "pe_ratio": "number",
    "pb_ratio": "number",
    "debt_to_equity": "number",
    "roe": "number"
  },
  "technical_analysis": "string",
  "risk_assessment": "string",
  "recommendation": "string (BUY|HOLD|SELL|AVOID)",
  "catalysts": "array of strings",
  "timestamp": "ISO date"
}
```

## How It Works
1. **Input Processing:** Receives stock symbol and context
2. **Analysis Generation:** Claude analyzes fundamentals and technicals
3. **Recommendation:** Generates BUY/HOLD/SELL/AVOID with reasoning
4. **Output Formatting:** Returns structured JSON response

## Use Cases
- Individual investor research
- Portfolio analysis
- Market screening
- Investment thesis development
- Financial education

## Limitations
- Historical data only (no real-time prices without integration)
- Requires manual stock symbol input
- No automated execution
- Not professional financial advice

## Best Practices
✓ Always verify findings with official sources
✓ Use multiple stocks for comparative analysis
✓ Update analysis periodically (quarterly)
✓ Combine with other research methods
✗ Don't use as sole investment decision factor

## Dependencies
- Claude AI (any version)
- Access to [Claude.ai](https://claude.ai) or Claude API

## Keywords
Stock analysis, Investment research, Financial analysis, Stock screening, 
AI-powered research, Fundamental analysis, Technical analysis
